  <h1>Lesson 17: Responsive Design in CSS</h1>
  <p>Learn How to Make Your Website Work on Mobile + Tablet + Desktop with Media Queries | LearnHTMLCSSJS.com</p>
</header>

<div class="container">
  <div class="tabs">
    <button id="lessonTabBtn" class="tab-btn active" onclick="showLesson()">📖 Lesson</button>
    <button id="testTabBtn" class="tab-btn" onclick="showTest()">📝 Test - 100 Marks</button>
  </div>
  <div id="lockMsg" class="lock-msg">🔒 Test is running! All tabs are locked until you submit the test or time ends.</div>

  <div id="lessonContent">
    <h2>1. What is Responsive Design?</h2>
    <p><b>Responsive Design</b> means your website <b>looks good on every screen</b> - Mobile, Tablet, and Desktop.</p>
    <p>Same website, different layout:</p>
    <p><b>Desktop:</b> 3 cards in one row.<br><b>Tablet:</b> 2 cards in one row.<br><b>Mobile:</b> 1 card in one row - full width.</p>
    <div class="note"><b>Why Important?</b> 80% people open websites on Mobile. If your website is not responsive, nobody will use it. Every client will ask for responsive design.</div>
    <h2>2. 3 Screen Sizes - Remember These</h2>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Device</th><th>Screen Width</th><th>Example</th></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Mobile</b></td><td>0 to 700px</td><td>Phone - 1 column</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Tablet</b></td><td>701px to 1024px</td><td>iPad - 2 columns</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Desktop</b></td><td>1025px and above</td><td>Laptop / PC - 3 columns</td></tr>
    </table>
    <div class="result"><b>Result - Same Cards on Different Screens:</b><p style="margin:8px 0 5px"><b>🖥️ Desktop - 3 Columns:</b></p><div style="display:flex;gap:10px"><div style="flex:1;background:#2563eb;color:white;padding:12px;border-radius:8px;text-align:center">Card 1</div><div style="flex:1;background:#16a34a;color:white;padding:12px;border-radius:8px;text-align:center">Card 2</div><div style="flex:1;background:#f59e0b;color:white;padding:12px;border-radius:8px;text-align:center">Card 3</div></div><p style="margin:10px 0 5px"><b>📱 Mobile - 1 Column (Stacked):</b></p><div style="background:#2563eb;color:white;padding:12px;border-radius:8px;margin:4px 0;text-align:center">Card 1</div><div style="background:#16a34a;color:white;padding:12px;border-radius:8px;margin:4px 0;text-align:center">Card 2</div><div style="background:#f59e0b;color:white;padding:12px;border-radius:8px;margin:4px 0;text-align:center">Card 3</div></div>
    <h2>3. Viewport Meta Tag - MUST Add</h2>
    <p>Without this tag, your website will look very small on mobile. <b>Always add this in &lt;head&gt;.</b></p>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;meta</span> <span class="attr">name</span>=<span class="val">"viewport"</span> <span class="attr">content</span>=<span class="val">"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="note"><b>Meaning:</b> width=device-width = Use full mobile width. initial-scale=1.0 = Do not zoom out.</div>
    <h2>4. Media Query - The Main Tool</h2>
    <p><b>Media Query</b> means: "If screen is this size, use this CSS."</p>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">/* Normal CSS - For Desktop */</span><br>
<span class="tag">.cards</span> <span class="text">{</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">display</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">flex</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">gap</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">15px</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span><br><br>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">/* Media Query - For Mobile (700px or smaller) */</span><br>
<span class="tag">@media</span> <span class="text">(</span><span class="attr">max-width</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">700px</span><span class="text">)</span> <span class="text">{</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">.cards</span> <span class="text">{</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">flex-direction</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">column</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">/* Stack cards one below other */</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">}</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">h1</span> <span class="text">{</span> <span class="attr">font-size</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">24px</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="text">}</span> <span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">/* Smaller heading on mobile */</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span>
    </code></div>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Part</th><th>Meaning</th></tr>
      <tr><td>@media</td><td>Start media query</td></tr>
      <tr><td>(max-width: 700px)</td><td>Only if screen is 700px or smaller</td></tr>
      <tr><td>{ ... }</td><td>CSS inside will only work on mobile</td></tr>
    </table>
    <h2>5. Responsive Grid - Best Trick</h2>
    <p>Use <b>auto-fit + minmax</b> - Grid automatically decides how many columns fit on screen. No media query needed!</p>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">.gallery</span> <span class="text">{</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">display</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">grid</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">grid-template-columns</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr))</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">gap</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">15px</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="note"><b>Meaning:</b> Each box minimum 250px. If screen is big, many boxes in one row. If screen is small, boxes go to next line automatically. This is the magic code for galleries!</div>
    <div class="result"><b>Result - Auto Responsive Gallery:</b><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(150px,1fr));gap:10px"><div style="background:#2563eb;color:white;padding:15px;border-radius:8px;text-align:center">Photo 1</div><div style="background:#16a34a;color:white;padding:15px;border-radius:8px;text-align:center">Photo 2</div><div style="background:#f59e0b;color:white;padding:15px;border-radius:8px;text-align:center">Photo 3</div><div style="background:#dc2626;color:white;padding:15px;border-radius:8px;text-align:center">Photo 4</div></div><p style="margin:8px 0 0">Try resizing your browser window - boxes will automatically move to next line!</p></div>
    <h2>6. Responsive Images & Text</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">/* Image never goes outside screen */</span><br>
<span class="tag">img</span> <span class="text">{</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">max-width</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">100%</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">height</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">auto</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span><br><br>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">/* Container never too wide */</span><br>
<span class="tag">.container</span> <span class="text">{</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">width</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">100%</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">max-width</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">1100px</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">margin</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">0 auto</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">padding</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">0 15px</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="note"><b>Golden Rules:</b> 1. Never use fixed width like width: 800px; for main boxes. Use width: 100%; + max-width: 1100px; 2. Always use flex-wrap: wrap; for Flexbox. 3. Always test on mobile - open your site on your phone.</div>
    <h2>7. Responsive Navbar - Desktop vs Mobile</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">/* Desktop Navbar - Side by Side */</span><br>
<span class="tag">.navbar</span> <span class="text">{</span> <span class="attr">display</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">flex</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="attr">justify-content</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">space-between</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="text">}</span><br><br>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">/* Mobile Navbar - Stacked */</span><br>
<span class="tag">@media</span> <span class="text">(</span><span class="attr">max-width</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">700px</span><span class="text">)</span> <span class="text">{</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">.navbar</span> <span class="text">{</span> <span class="attr">flex-direction</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">column</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="attr">text-align</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">center</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="text">}</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="result"><b>Result:</b><div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;background:#0f172a;color:white;padding:12px 15px;border-radius:8px"><b>My Website</b><span>Home | About | Contact</span></div><p style="margin:8px 0 0">On Mobile (700px or smaller), this navbar becomes stacked - Logo on top, Menu below.</p></div>
    <h2>8. Full Example - Responsive Cards (Copy This)</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">.cards</span> <span class="text">{</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">display</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">flex</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">gap</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">15px</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">flex-wrap</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">wrap</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span><br>
<span class="tag">.card</span> <span class="text">{</span> <span class="attr">flex</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">1</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="attr">min-width</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">250px</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="text">}</span><br><br>
<span class="tag">@media</span> <span class="text">(</span><span class="attr">max-width</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">700px</span><span class="text">)</span> <span class="text">{</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">.cards</span> <span class="text">{</span> <span class="attr">flex-direction</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">column</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="text">}</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">h1</span> <span class="text">{</span> <span class="attr">font-size</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">24px</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="text">}</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>9. Homework - Practice for 2 Minutes</h2>
    <p>In Playground, make this:</p>
    <p>1. One <b>Navbar</b> - flex, space-between on desktop, column on mobile (700px media query)<br>2. Three <b>Cards</b> - flex, side by side on desktop, stacked on mobile<br>3. One <b>Gallery</b> - grid with repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr))</p>
    <div class="box"><b>Remember:</b> Responsive = Looks good on Mobile + Tablet + Desktop | Viewport Meta Tag = Always add | Media Query = @media (max-width: 700px) { ... } | max-width = 700px or smaller | Mobile = 0-700px, Tablet = 701-1024px, Desktop = 1025px+ | Auto Grid = repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr)) | img { max-width: 100%; } | Container = width: 100%; max-width: 1100px;</div>
    <p><b>Next Step:</b> After this lesson, go to <a href="/lesson18">Lesson 18 - Buttons & Links Styling</a> to learn hover effects, beautiful buttons and links.</p>
    <a id="playgroundLink" class="btn" href="/playground">▶ Try it Yourself - Playground</a><br><br>
