          <div class="question"><b>Q1. Responsive Design means?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q1" value="a"> Website looks good on Mobile + Tablet + Desktop</label><label><input type="radio" name="q1" value="b"> Website only for Desktop</label><label><input type="radio" name="q1" value="c"> Website only for Mobile</label><label><input type="radio" name="q1" value="d"> Website with no CSS</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q2. Which tag MUST be added for Responsive?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q2" value="a"> &lt;meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"&gt;</label><label><input type="radio" name="q2" value="b"> &lt;meta name="color"&gt;</label><label><input type="radio" name="q2" value="c"> &lt;meta name="responsive"&gt;</label><label><input type="radio" name="q2" value="d"> &lt;meta name="mobile"&gt;</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q3. What is correct Media Query syntax?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q3" value="a"> @media (max-width: 700px) { ... }</label><label><input type="radio" name="q3" value="b"> @media 700px { ... }</label><label><input type="radio" name="q3" value="c"> media (700px) { ... }</label><label><input type="radio" name="q3" value="d"> @query (700px) { ... }</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q4. Mobile screen size is?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q4" value="a"> 0 to 700px</label><label><input type="radio" name="q4" value="b"> 1025px and above</label><label><input type="radio" name="q4" value="c"> 701 to 1024px</label><label><input type="radio" name="q4" value="d"> 2000px and above</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q5. Desktop screen size is?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q5" value="a"> 1025px and above</label><label><input type="radio" name="q5" value="b"> 0 to 700px</label><label><input type="radio" name="q5" value="c"> 701 to 1024px</label><label><input type="radio" name="q5" value="d"> 0 to 300px</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q6. Which code makes Auto Responsive Gallery?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q6" value="a"> grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr));</label><label><input type="radio" name="q6" value="b"> grid-template-columns: 3;</label><label><input type="radio" name="q6" value="c"> display: flex;</label><label><input type="radio" name="q6" value="d"> grid-template-columns: 250px;</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q7. How to make Image Responsive?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q7" value="a"> img { max-width: 100%; height: auto; }</label><label><input type="radio" name="q7" value="b"> img { width: 1000px; }</label><label><input type="radio" name="q7" value="c"> img { width: 500px; height: 500px; }</label><label><input type="radio" name="q7" value="d"> img { max-width: 0; }</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q8. On Mobile, 3 cards should become?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q8" value="a"> 1 Column - Stacked one below other</label><label><input type="radio" name="q8" value="b"> Still 3 columns</label><label><input type="radio" name="q8" value="c"> Hidden</label><label><input type="radio" name="q8" value="d"> 10 columns</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q9. Which is correct for Container?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q9" value="a"> width: 100%; max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto;</label><label><input type="radio" name="q9" value="b"> width: 2000px;</label><label><input type="radio" name="q9" value="c"> width: 100px;</label><label><input type="radio" name="q9" value="d"> width: 0;</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q10. In Media Query, max-width: 700px means?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q10" value="a"> CSS works only if screen is 700px or smaller</label><label><input type="radio" name="q10" value="b"> CSS works only if screen is bigger than 700px</label><label><input type="radio" name="q10" value="c"> CSS works always</label><label><input type="radio" name="q10" value="d"> CSS never works</label></div>
